How about this: a ring, when worn sufficiently long, will have an adverse
permanent effect. 

Eg, a ring of gain strength, if worn long enough, will _reduce_ the
natural strength when removed. Like if your strength is 10, and you
wear a ring +3 of gain str long enough, your strength will
be 13 when the ring is worn, but will go down to _7_ when
removed.

Also, a ring of fire resistance removes _intrinsic_ fire resistance,
a ring of conflict either makes you aggressive (ie, NH won't ask you
before you attack a peaceful creature) or aggravates monsters..

This idea will need further work: 1) to make sure it makes a difference,
and 2) to avoid loopholes that might cause it to become easier, by `cheating'.
It has the advantage of being `natural' to some degree, and maybe will
be relatively easy to code up.
